{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And whenever the cloud was taken up.</b> So fixed was the dwelling of the Shekhinah in the Mishkan that it would never depart from there at all — until Israel needed to journey. This was not so in Shiloh, nor in the First Temple, nor in the Second. But even more than this shall be in the Third Temple, may it be rebuilt and established speedily in our days, as it says: וַאֲנִי אֶהְיֶה לָּהּ נְאֻם ה' חוֹמַת אֵשׁ סָבִיב וּלְכָבוֹד אֶהְיֶה בְתוֹכָהּ (Zechariah 2:9). Thus concludes the section Pekudei."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:27.058638569Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}